1
00:00:00,827 --> 00:00:06,444
Are you perhaps Kazumi Hojo's friend?

2
00:00:06,444 --> 00:00:07,589
Huh?

3
00:00:08,464 --> 00:00:12,392
Oh, I'm his younger brother, Koki.
Nice to meet you.

4
00:00:12,392 --> 00:00:15,200
I'm Kazumi Hojo's brother.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:18,025
Oh, his brother...

6
00:00:18,025 --> 00:00:21,613
Nice to meet you. I'm Himari Shibasaki.

7
00:00:26,905 --> 00:00:31,117
Wait, did you two
have a fight or something?

8
00:00:32,453 --> 00:00:34,522
Well, just a small one.

9
00:00:34,522 --> 00:00:39,922
Wow, picking a fight with that guy...
You've got guts.

10
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:33,134
Sorry to impose,
but could you give this to him?

11
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:35,304
No, something this important should be...

12
00:01:35,304 --> 00:01:38,111
No, just tell him it's for Mom.

13
00:01:38,111 --> 00:01:39,931
Sorry, please.

14
00:01:41,395 --> 00:01:44,655
Can't you return it yourself?

15
00:01:46,891 --> 00:01:48,216
I'd rather not.

16
00:01:49,111 --> 00:01:52,271
I don't want to see her
or even send her anything.

17
00:01:53,064 --> 00:01:58,662
Honestly, it's not just my mom.
I don't like seeing my brother either.

18
00:01:58,662 --> 00:02:01,422
Our family doesn't get along.

19
00:02:02,391 --> 00:02:04,967
I see.

20
00:02:05,747 --> 00:02:08,448
Our parents' relationship was a mess.

21
00:02:08,448 --> 00:02:12,677
He kept trying to mediate,
always walking on eggshells.

22
00:02:12,677 --> 00:02:14,806
Walking on eggshells?

23
00:02:14,806 --> 00:02:19,850
He'd go back and forth between them,
agreeing with whatever they'd say.

24
00:02:20,629 --> 00:02:23,034
He's good at it.

25
00:02:23,034 --> 00:02:26,207
He gets along with everyone, you know?

26
00:02:27,089 --> 00:02:31,897
Well, I guess he does have a lot of friends.

27
00:02:31,897 --> 00:02:33,743
It's a skill.

28
00:02:33,743 --> 00:02:38,953
Putting on a fake smile
and saying what people want to hear.

29
00:02:38,953 --> 00:02:41,959
So he'd get along with anyone.

30
00:02:41,959 --> 00:02:47,260
But I don't think
he ever had any real friends.

31
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:51,364
You think so?

32
00:02:51,364 --> 00:02:53,725
He's hard to read, isn't he?

33
00:02:55,096 --> 00:02:57,175
He's always been like that.

34
00:02:59,083 --> 00:03:03,075
But he never seemed that way to me.

35
00:03:06,747 --> 00:03:10,855
That's probably because it's you.

36
00:03:10,855 --> 00:03:12,033
Huh?

37
00:03:13,069 --> 00:03:17,305
He'd try to get along with me too,
and strike up conversations.

38
00:03:17,305 --> 00:03:20,449
Honestly, I'd get annoyed and ignore him.

39
00:03:20,449 --> 00:03:24,838
But there was one moment
when he seemed different.

40
00:03:24,838 --> 00:03:26,315
Back in college,

41
00:03:26,315 --> 00:03:29,843
<i>he showed me a photo and said,
"I made an interesting friend".</i>

42
00:03:29,843 --> 00:03:33,571
His smile was so genuine.

43
00:03:33,571 --> 00:03:35,774
That's how it looked to me.

44
00:03:36,810 --> 00:03:40,229
And the person in that photo was...

45
00:03:41,297 --> 00:03:43,057
Me?

46
00:03:43,057 --> 00:03:48,863
I know it's not my place to say,
but please keep being his friend.

47
00:03:52,381 --> 00:03:55,565
Well, I'll be going then.

48
00:03:55,565 --> 00:03:57,826
Give him that bankbook, okay?

49
00:03:57,826 --> 00:03:59,904
Got it.

50
00:04:05,157 --> 00:04:09,985
<i>So, Kazumi doesn't get along with his family.</i>

51
00:04:09,985 --> 00:04:14,055
Then should we go back to being friends?

52
00:04:15,551 --> 00:04:19,644
<i>Why did he say that?</i>

53
00:04:21,719 --> 00:04:24,586
I need to talk to Kazumi properly.

54
00:04:34,951 --> 00:04:37,647
Good morning.

55
00:04:38,535 --> 00:04:40,394
Good morning.

56
00:04:42,889 --> 00:04:46,315
Do you have a minute?

57
00:04:46,315 --> 00:04:50,185
Yeah, sure. Is this about Yanami?

58
00:04:53,427 --> 00:04:55,208
Yeah.

59
00:04:55,208 --> 00:04:57,524
I'll talk to the chief.

60
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:04,564
But before that,
can I chat with you and Nihei together?

61
00:05:05,484 --> 00:05:06,849
Yes.

62
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:19,896
Do you have a little time tonight?

63
00:05:22,664 --> 00:05:27,940
Sorry, some work piled up during my trip.
Might be difficult.

64
00:05:30,844 --> 00:05:32,690
I see.

65
00:05:35,991 --> 00:05:38,031
Hojo! Long time no see!

66
00:05:38,031 --> 00:05:40,555
- Good morning, Ando.
- Hello.

67
00:05:40,555 --> 00:05:42,477
How was Fukuoka?

68
00:05:47,904 --> 00:05:50,360
<i>He's avoiding me.</i>

69
00:05:52,464 --> 00:05:56,454
<i>I wanted to support him,</i>

70
00:05:57,310 --> 00:06:00,149
<i>but I caused him trouble instead.</i>

71
00:06:00,778 --> 00:06:03,327
<i>What am I even doing?</i>

72
00:06:03,327 --> 00:06:07,084
Is that okay with you, Shibasaki?

73
00:06:08,091 --> 00:06:11,238
Yes, thank you.

74
00:06:11,238 --> 00:06:14,634
Okay, everyone, please handle your parts.

75
00:06:20,559 --> 00:06:24,370
Nihei, I want you
to apologize to Yanami properly.

76
00:06:24,370 --> 00:06:25,967
Can we go together?

77
00:06:25,967 --> 00:06:28,211
Yes, I understand.

78
00:06:34,089 --> 00:06:41,619
<i>I lost my lover and my best friend.</i>

79
00:06:44,106 --> 00:06:46,246
Sorry for the wait.

80
00:06:46,246 --> 00:06:47,356
All right, let's go.

81
00:06:47,356 --> 00:06:48,803
Okay.

82
00:06:53,363 --> 00:06:57,102
We sincerely apologize for the trouble.

83
00:07:00,108 --> 00:07:02,755
Let's take a look now.

84
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:04,091
Okay.

85
00:07:05,145 --> 00:07:06,872
Here it is.

86
00:07:11,823 --> 00:07:13,552
Excuse me.

87
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:20,031
Sorry I'm late.

88
00:07:20,031 --> 00:07:22,594
My other meeting ran late.

89
00:07:23,554 --> 00:07:26,203
Hojo? Is something wrong?

90
00:07:26,203 --> 00:07:30,443
Well, I already heard
from Shibasaki and Nihei,

91
00:07:30,443 --> 00:07:33,983
but I thought
I should hear both sides directly.

92
00:07:33,983 --> 00:07:36,016
Excuse me?

93
00:07:36,016 --> 00:07:39,095
I heard there's been
a lot of back-and-forth on your end.

94
00:07:39,095 --> 00:07:42,000
I can only imagine the stress.

95
00:07:44,663 --> 00:07:49,387
But pushing all those
last-minute changes onto us

96
00:07:49,387 --> 00:07:52,023
seems a bit heavy-handed, doesn't it?

97
00:07:59,472 --> 00:08:02,573
I'm sure they could have done better,

98
00:08:02,573 --> 00:08:07,050
but Shibasaki and Nihei
worked hard on this new proposal.

99
00:08:07,050 --> 00:08:12,501
I would really appreciate it
if you could look with an open mind.

100
00:08:15,791 --> 00:08:18,197
I'm glad it went well.

101
00:08:18,197 --> 00:08:22,181
Hojo, you were moving
behind the scenes too, huh?

102
00:08:22,181 --> 00:08:25,782
It's not that big a deal.

103
00:08:25,782 --> 00:08:29,225
I just got some insider info
from an acquaintance.

104
00:08:29,225 --> 00:08:31,751
Why did you do that?

105
00:08:31,751 --> 00:08:36,258
Isn't it natural to help your team
when you are struggling?

106
00:08:37,165 --> 00:08:39,209
Still not convinced?

107
00:08:39,209 --> 00:08:40,809
I don't mean that.

108
00:08:42,517 --> 00:08:46,488
I was just thinking
it wasn't entirely our fault after all.

109
00:08:47,767 --> 00:08:49,251
Yeah.

110
00:08:49,251 --> 00:08:54,121
But I do understand there are times
when you have to bow your head anyway.

111
00:08:54,121 --> 00:08:56,858
That's on me.

112
00:08:57,601 --> 00:09:03,123
This could've been prevented
if I had called him out from the start.

113
00:09:04,231 --> 00:09:06,871
I'm really sorry.

114
00:09:06,871 --> 00:09:09,923
I know I'm the one at fault,

115
00:09:09,923 --> 00:09:11,927
so please don't apologize.

116
00:09:20,019 --> 00:09:23,280
Sorry, I'm going to get a drink.

117
00:09:46,078 --> 00:09:50,935
It'll be okay.
I'm sure Nihei will understand.

118
00:09:54,479 --> 00:09:56,196
Yeah.

119
00:10:00,849 --> 00:10:04,371
You feel frustrated and apologetic

120
00:10:04,371 --> 00:10:08,409
about having Nihei apologize, right?

121
00:10:09,685 --> 00:10:12,818
And you didn't want to rely on me either,
did you?

122
00:10:14,252 --> 00:10:18,902
You didn't want to worry me.

123
00:10:22,845 --> 00:10:27,218
<i>Kazumi has always been there for me.</i>

124
00:10:29,059 --> 00:10:31,488
I'll head back first, then.

125
00:10:31,488 --> 00:10:33,644
<i>Things can't stay this way.</i>

126
00:10:34,727 --> 00:10:36,072
<i>I have to...</i>

127
00:10:36,072 --> 00:10:37,771
Kazumi!

128
00:10:42,375 --> 00:10:48,228
Want to go to Hamagasaki Beach this weekend?

129
00:10:48,953 --> 00:10:51,160
We promised to go.

130
00:10:55,005 --> 00:11:00,032
I want... to have a heart-to-heart there.

131
00:11:01,389 --> 00:11:06,492
I want to know you better.

132
00:11:21,225 --> 00:11:26,195
This is from your brother.

133
00:11:30,397 --> 00:11:32,194
Koki?

134
00:11:32,194 --> 00:11:34,039
Yeah.

135
00:11:34,039 --> 00:11:36,818
He said to give it back to your mom.

136
00:11:39,355 --> 00:11:41,570
When I met him,

137
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:47,883
he told me a little bit about your family.

138
00:11:48,933 --> 00:11:50,427
Huh?

139
00:11:52,041 --> 00:11:57,219
I didn't know anything...

140
00:11:58,164 --> 00:12:00,676
about your struggles...

141
00:12:01,708 --> 00:12:03,941
and your burdens.

142
00:12:07,573 --> 00:12:12,646
And when you said yesterday
that we should go back to being friends,

143
00:12:13,389 --> 00:12:15,144
it confused me.

144
00:12:17,966 --> 00:12:22,641
So please, tell me about yourself.

145
00:12:26,684 --> 00:12:29,404
I can't tell you.

146
00:12:32,781 --> 00:12:34,960
But I want to know.

147
00:12:37,177 --> 00:12:39,984
I know it's selfish,

148
00:12:39,984 --> 00:12:43,677
but I don't want anyone else but you.

149
00:12:44,911 --> 00:12:47,509
I want you to stay as my lover.

150
00:12:49,051 --> 00:12:50,713
So...

151
00:12:52,485 --> 00:12:54,140
I'll be waiting.

152
00:12:56,552 --> 00:12:58,763
I'm sorry. I should get back.

153
00:13:15,743 --> 00:13:18,265
Shouldn't you go after him?

154
00:13:20,944 --> 00:13:23,131
Were you listening?

155
00:13:25,838 --> 00:13:29,193
You totally shut me down, huh?

156
00:13:31,028 --> 00:13:32,904
I'm sorry.

157
00:13:35,428 --> 00:13:37,200
Don't apologize.

158
00:13:38,235 --> 00:13:42,465
I want you to keep smiling.

159
00:13:44,111 --> 00:13:46,585
I hope you two can work things out.

160
00:13:50,125 --> 00:13:53,050
Thank you, Nihei.

161
00:13:54,916 --> 00:13:56,553
Yeah.

162
00:13:59,179 --> 00:14:02,239
The client reacted really well
to that proposal.

163
00:14:02,239 --> 00:14:05,062
Really? That's great.

164
00:14:09,208 --> 00:14:12,995
That was all thanks to everyone helping out.

165
00:14:12,995 --> 00:14:18,746
<i>All this time...
Everything Kazumi has done for me...</i>

166
00:14:18,746 --> 00:14:22,371
<i>Now it's my turn to return the favor.</i>

167
00:15:16,087 --> 00:15:18,135
Maybe he's not coming.

168
00:15:35,952 --> 00:15:37,549
Kazumi.

169
00:15:38,389 --> 00:15:41,659
Sorry I'm late.

170
00:15:42,782 --> 00:15:44,328
It's fine.

171
00:16:00,962 --> 00:16:02,511
This place...

172
00:16:03,716 --> 00:16:06,880
It's the last place I came to with my mom.

173
00:16:08,216 --> 00:16:12,839
I come here sometimes when I miss her.

174
00:16:13,937 --> 00:16:18,445
When I'm happy. Or when I'm lonely.

175
00:16:22,846 --> 00:16:28,026
I always wanted to come here
with the person I love.

176
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:31,792
Because I wanted to show my mom too.

177
00:16:37,337 --> 00:16:40,112
When I first saw you,

178
00:16:41,084 --> 00:16:44,501
you were smiling gently
at the flowers in the flower bed.

179
00:16:46,059 --> 00:16:48,569
Seeing that,

180
00:16:48,569 --> 00:16:51,756
I knew I wanted to be friends with you.

181
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,870
You know...

182
00:16:58,442 --> 00:17:01,123
when I talked about my family,

183
00:17:01,123 --> 00:17:06,762
you said, "I bet she was a wonderful mother".

184
00:17:06,762 --> 00:17:08,986
Do you remember that?

185
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:10,309
Did I say that?

186
00:17:10,309 --> 00:17:12,320
Yeah.

187
00:17:12,320 --> 00:17:19,323
That moment, I realized I want to be
lifelong friends with this person.

188
00:17:29,766 --> 00:17:35,727
So when you said, "Let's stop being friends",

189
00:17:35,727 --> 00:17:38,066
I was at a total loss.

190
00:17:39,188 --> 00:17:43,409
Sorry, I came off a bit strong, huh?

191
00:17:50,904 --> 00:17:55,197
<i>I was pretty nervous on our first date.</i>

192
00:17:55,197 --> 00:17:57,583
<i>I agonized over what to wear.</i>

193
00:17:57,583 --> 00:18:03,493
<i>Me too. I was actually nervous
when I held your hand.</i>

194
00:18:03,493 --> 00:18:10,281
<i>When I saw you with Okada, I got jealous.</i>

195
00:18:10,281 --> 00:18:14,224
<i>I knew Nihei liked you.</i>

196
00:18:14,224 --> 00:18:16,297
<i>Oh, really?</i>

197
00:18:16,297 --> 00:18:21,364
<i>When Nihei told me he liked me,
my heart skipped a beat.</i>

198
00:18:21,364 --> 00:18:24,871
<i>I mean, he was so sincere about it.</i>

199
00:18:24,871 --> 00:18:27,518
<i>I see.</i>

200
00:18:27,518 --> 00:18:31,578
<i>I was scared he might
take you away from me.</i>

201
00:18:37,177 --> 00:18:39,085
When I was a kid,

202
00:18:40,243 --> 00:18:43,219
I overheard my dad on the phone.

203
00:18:45,991 --> 00:18:51,943
I asked my mom, "Who is this Mana person
that Dad keeps calling"?

204
00:18:51,943 --> 00:18:53,956
"Why is he saying he loves her"?

205
00:18:59,044 --> 00:19:03,944
From that day on, everything changed.

206
00:19:10,382 --> 00:19:13,529
I broke something precious.

207
00:19:13,529 --> 00:19:15,527
It was my fault.

208
00:19:19,273 --> 00:19:25,625
That's why I always thought
I couldn't make anyone happy.

209
00:19:31,773 --> 00:19:36,351
But then I met you.

210
00:19:41,752 --> 00:19:45,729
Someday, you'll love someone,

211
00:19:45,729 --> 00:19:48,935
get married, and start a family.

212
00:19:50,281 --> 00:19:53,362
I hoped that someone could be me.

213
00:19:55,472 --> 00:19:59,706
But one day,
I'd break something precious again.

214
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:05,338
I'm afraid I'd hurt you.

215
00:20:19,238 --> 00:20:22,182
That's why I said we should just be friends.

216
00:20:30,705 --> 00:20:34,981
Thank you for telling me.

217
00:20:38,967 --> 00:20:40,778
You're so silly.

218
00:20:41,790 --> 00:20:46,546
Do you really think
we'd fall apart that easily?

219
00:20:49,435 --> 00:20:54,369
As long as you're happy, that's enough.

220
00:20:55,277 --> 00:20:57,348
Even if it's not me.

221
00:21:02,684 --> 00:21:04,552
You're wrong.

222
00:21:05,785 --> 00:21:08,610
Because then you're not there.

223
00:21:16,870 --> 00:21:18,786
Are you sure?

224
00:21:20,921 --> 00:21:22,695
What about you?

225
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:26,128
What do you want?

226
00:21:31,930 --> 00:21:34,749
I want to be the one closest to you.

227
00:21:35,987 --> 00:21:40,313
I want you to be in my future.

228
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:49,818
Then if I'm with you, you'll be happy?

229
00:21:50,787 --> 00:21:52,160
Yeah.

230
00:21:59,596 --> 00:22:01,705
Good answer.

231
00:22:10,348 --> 00:22:15,984
I'll make you happy.

232
00:22:21,206 --> 00:22:22,886
So...

233
00:22:26,424 --> 00:22:29,929
now it's your turn to be happy.

234
00:22:32,661 --> 00:22:39,330
So, we'll end our friendship now, right?

235
00:22:39,330 --> 00:22:40,783
Yeah.

236
00:23:42,707 --> 00:23:45,576
This drama is a work of fiction.
